From 747111791a5e24f26a6939a3acc34a7ef7ccc7b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:03:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] port 5549a72b bda03b22 c50cdf98 9db053af 90f73293: serve:
 admission by estimated new tokens (opt-in STRATA_ADMIT_BY_NEW=1) and the
 yield to short requests with top-row park slots and YIELDNO retry (opt-in
 STRATA_YIELD_SHORT=N), STRATA_YIELDS_MAX

Ported as one rewritten unit (the 0.1.44 entry [est, arrival, ordered, total,
ids, cache] clashes with v0.2.12's [plen, arrival, new, prompt, request] that
STRATA_COALESCE_PREFILL reads at e[3]/e[4]).

Adaptations against v0.2.12:
- WaitEntry: a list subclass that keeps upstream's five positions and adds the
  named fields total / ids / held (cached new tokens) beside them; compared by
  identity, so `entry in wait_lens` never compares prompts.  ids is kept only
  with STRATA_YIELD_SHORT, as before.  _entry_new reads named fields; any plain
  list entry counts its e[0].
- _take_control: upstream signature (prompt=, unadmitted=, queue deadline,
  #4738 re-check) plus total= / since= / ids=.  The turn test is one local
  may_go() used both before acquire() and in the #4738 re-check, so the
  "paused read lets the whole short burst go first" rule can not spin
  (it is only evaluated with YIELD_SHORT > 0 and an engine saying read_yield=1).
- BYIELD goes out through _send_for(born, ...) (#4451); YIELDNO is parsed next
  to YIELDED; _yield_no / _yield_no_final / _own_est are _RequestOwned.
- admitted() fires once (a non-blocking lock) at the solo GEN, at the BGEN
  (the COALESCE preslot path included) and, with STRATA_COALESCE_PREFILL, from
  _coalesce on the leader's thread when the follower's BCO line goes out.
- Back from waiting for a slot: with ADMIT_BY_NEW and nothing generated, it asks
  again new=True + unadmitted=True with its estimate and first arrival
  (9db053af); otherwise upstream's unadmitted=not out call.
- The park slot remembers its engine process (park_gen); free_park() only
  touches slot_busy of that process.  A solo read paused into `park` skips the
  #1869 carry_leg (its leg is in upstream's yielded_legs like any give-way);
  both park continue paths append to yielded_legs.
- yslot= rides as its own BGEN key (v0.2.12 has no waiting= key; 7fcea102 is
  dropped).
- StrataEngine.YIELDS_MAX = STRATA_YIELDS_MAX (unset: upstream's 2), also
  without STRATA_YIELD_SHORT.
- admit_env() keeps upstream's ADMIT_SHORT_FIRST / ADMIT_MAX_WAIT_S names and
  values when STRATA_ADMIT_BY_NEW is unset; load_counts / load_view add the
  admit_by_new block on top of upstream's resuming/coalesced counts.
- Tests: serve/test_read_yield.py and serve/test_admit_est.py use WaitEntry
  instead of index lists (SlotsBusy reads .total, sets slot_q for v0.2.12's
  generate_batched).  serve/test_admit_order.py keeps upstream's cases
  unchanged and adds three (entry layout, unset switches leave order and #656
  rule alone, a paused read lets every short request go first).

Unset STRATA_ADMIT_BY_NEW / STRATA_YIELD_SHORT / STRATA_YIELDS_MAX: the order,
the give-way and every line sent equal stock v0.2.12.  Set against an engine
without STRATA_READ_YIELD (no INFO read_yield=1): the #656 rule and slots as
stock (no park, no yslot=, nothing waits for a YIELDNO); ADMIT_BY_NEW only
changes the order.

